# Basic Honeypots Deployment Documentation

## Overview

This document describes the deployment and testing process of the basic honeypot environment used in the Smart Honeypot Orchestrator & Threat Intelligence Dashboard project.

The deployed honeypots are:

| Honeypot | Type | Purpose | Port |
|---|---|---|---|
| Cowrie | SSH Honeypot | Capture SSH attacks and attacker commands | 22/tcp |
| Dionaea | FTP Honeypot | Capture malware-related activity and FTP attacks | 21/tcp |
| Tanner + Snare | HTTP Honeypot | Capture web-based attacks and suspicious requests | 80/tcp |

---

# Deployment Structure

The deployment is organized using Docker Compose.

Project structure:

```text
docker/

├── docker-compose.yml
│
├── cowrie/
│   ├── docker-compose.yml
│   └── data/
│
├── dionaea/
│   ├── docker-compose.yml
│   └── data/
│
└── tanner/
    ├── docker-compose.yml
    ├── snare/
    ├── tanner/
    ├── redis/
    └── phpox/
```

The main compose file starts all honeypots:

```yaml
include:
  - ./cowrie/docker-compose.yml
  - ./dionaea/docker-compose.yml
  - ./tanner/docker-compose.yml
```

---

# Running Honeypots

Start all honeypots:

```bash
docker compose up -d
```

Check running containers:

```bash
docker ps
```

